{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>This is the matter that HaShem commanded.</b> One should not say that 'commanded' here is an absolute command that each and every one not gather except a precise omer, for if so, they did not fulfill the command, since they took from the measure more or less, and it says 'and the children of Israel did so.' Rather, 'commanded' here means as in 'ויעמוד איש' — *establir* in the vernacular, i.e., a statute; and for measuring — even if one gathers two omers, when he comes home and measures he will find only a precise omer. And if his fellow gathered only half an omer, when he comes home and measures he will find a full omer."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:12.810230814Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}